The fresh rebuild closes the sole positive claim with `#Top` and exit 0. Static review found one proof-local acceleration: a specialized `[2:]` string-slice equation. Ground fixed-vs-extended probes, including an observable continuation and an out-of-match `[1:]` case, agree; the equation is mathematically sound, but the candidate provides no bridge-free universal K connection theorem. I’m recording that as an evidence limitation, not an unsoundness claim.
